<title>CHILE: Chile Quebrada Blanca copper miners to vote again.</title>
<headline>Chile Quebrada Blanca copper miners to vote again.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Chile's Quebrada Blanca copper mine will vote Wednesday afternoon on a new pay offer from the company in last-minute talks to avert a strike at the pit, said a company official.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be a vote in the afternoon on the new offer,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>She did not know details of the latest proposals.</p>
<p>Around 300 workers at the mine rejected the company's earlier pay offer in a ballot Sunday and were due to strike from first shift Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Vancouver-based Cominco Ltd, Cominco Resources and Teck Resources International hold a 76.5 percent stake in Quebrada Blanca which produces 75,000 tonnes of copper cathodes a year.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
